; OVERVIEW
; Bank 5: the second half of the CE-1600P's 32 KB ROM, seen at 4000H-7FFFH when page 1
; selects bank 5. It holds two ROM modules of 8 KB each, both found by the P0-B0 module
; scan (ROM4MAP):
;   4000H-5FFFH  CE-1600F floppy driver: devices X: and Y:, disk IOCS 80H..89H (module +08H),
;                FILE functions (module +15H, same FAT-like file system as the bank-3 RAM
;                disk), boot from disk, INIT "X:" (format) and a disk-copy routine.
;   6000H-7FFFH  cassette (CE-152 through the CE-1600P): device CAS:, the keywords CHAIN,
;                CLOAD, CSAVE, MERGE, RMT and two more, and the CAS: file functions.
; The work area of the floppy module is at F038H (EXROMWK area 5, 428H bytes; IY =
; work+411H), the drive controller ports are 78H.. (drive X) / 70H.. (drive Y).
; ============================================================================

; ---- I/O ports ----
P_LH10:     equ 10H     ; LH-5811 compatible block 10H-1FH (base)
